424 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Proposition delivered well-crafted arguments that focused on the broader picture. They argued that endangered species constitute a part of the animal population, and while it was agreed that endangered species deserve help, the Proposition claimed them to have equal rights to welfare as all other animals. Further, they boldly stated that using limited financial resources on endangered species was gambling rather than investing, since their chances of survival are not concrete. The government put immense emphasis on the need for policies that are sustainable and feasible in the long term, in order to prevent further extinction of species. This was beautifully highlighted in an idiom - "We should not put all of our eggs in one basket".The Proposition concluded that prioritizing all our resources for the conservation of dying species may cause a wider collapse in the natural ecosystem.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
